Here are the full contents of all 5 files:

---

## 1. `app/welcome.tsx`

```tsx
import React, { useState, useEffect } from 'react';
import { View, Text, StyleSheet, TouchableOpacity } from 'react-native';
import { SafeAreaView } from 'react-native-safe-area-context';
import { useRouter } from 'expo-router';
import { colors, commonStyles, buttonStyles } from '@/styles/commonStyles';
import { loadProfile } from '@/utils/storage';
import PaywallScreen from '@/components/PaywallScreen';
import { useSubscription } from '@/contexts/SubscriptionContext';
import AppLogo from '@/components/AppLogo';

export default function WelcomeScreen() {
  const router = useRouter();
  const { isSubscribed, refreshSubscription } = useSubscription();
  const [showPaywall, setShowPaywall] = useState(false);

  // If user becomes subscribed while on this screen, redirect them
  useEffect(() => {
    if (isSubscribed) {
      loadProfile().then((profile) => {
        const hasCompleteProfile = profile && profile.portionTargets;
        if (hasCompleteProfile) {
          router.replace('/(tabs)/(home)');
        } else {
          router.replace('/setup-profile');
        }
      });
    }
  }, [isSubscribed, router]);

  const handleStartTrial = () => {
    console.log('User tapped Start Your Free Trial button');
    setShowPaywall(true);
  };

  const handlePaywallDismiss = async () => {
    setShowPaywall(false);
    await refreshSubscription();
  };

  return (
    <SafeAreaView style={styles.container}>
      <View style={styles.content}>
        <View style={styles.header}>
          <AppLogo size={80} />
          <Text style={styles.title}>Welcome to Portion Track</Text>
          <Text style={styles.subtitle}>Simple Portions. Balanced Eating.</Text>
          <Text style={styles.description}>A simple way to eat well and build healthy habits for life.</Text>
        </View>
        <TouchableOpacity style={[buttonStyles.primary, styles.button]} onPress={handleStartTrial}>
          <Text style={buttonStyles.primaryText}>Start Your Free Trial</Text>
        </TouchableOpacity>
      </View>
      <PaywallScreen visible={showPaywall} onDismiss={handlePaywallDismiss} canDismiss={true} />
    </SafeAreaView>
  );
}
```

**Key behavior:**
- On mount, if `isSubscribed` is already `true` → redirects to `/(tabs)/(home)` or `/setup-profile`
- "Start Your Free Trial" button → shows `<PaywallScreen>` modal
- On paywall dismiss → calls `refreshSubscription()`, then the `useEffect` handles navigation if purchase succeeded

---

## 2. `contexts/SubscriptionContext.tsx`

```tsx
// isSubscribed defaults to false, isLoading defaults to true
// refreshSubscription() is the main method

// DEV MODE BYPASS (critical!):
if (__DEV__) {
  setIsSubscribed(true);  // Auto-grants subscription in dev/preview
  return;
}

// Production: reads from AsyncStorage via loadSubscriptionStatus()
// Also listens to subscriptionEmitter for real-time updates from purchase listener
```

**Key behavior:**
- **`__DEV__` bypass**: In development/preview, `isSubscribed` is **always `true`** — the paywall is completely skipped
- In production: reads `AsyncStorage` via `loadSubscriptionStatus()`
- Exports `subscriptionEmitter` (EventEmitter) so `subscriptionManager` can push real-time updates without polling
- `SUBSCRIPTION_UPDATED_EVENT` listener immediately calls `setIsSubscribed(subscribed)` when a purchase completes

---

## 3. `app/_layout.tsx`

**Key behavior:**
- `initialRouteName` is determined by `hasProfile`:
  - Profile exists → starts at `(tabs)`
  - No profile → starts at `welcome`
- **No subscription gate here** — the layout only checks for profile existence
- `SubscriptionProvider` wraps `AppContent`
- Fonts, splash screen, notifications, and backup are initialized here

**Critical gap:** If a user has a profile but no subscription (production), `_layout.tsx` routes them directly to `(tabs)` — **bypassing the welcome/paywall screen entirely**.

---

## 4. `app/(tabs)/_layout.tsx`

```tsx
// Pure navigation layout — no paywall gate
// Uses FloatingTabBar with 6 tabs: Track, History, Weight, FAQs, Profile, Settings
// Stack with headerShown: false, animation: 'none'
```

**Key behavior:** No subscription check whatsoever. Any user who reaches `(tabs)` has full access.

---

## 5. `utils/subscriptionManager.ts`

**Key behavior:**
- iOS-only via `expo-in-app-purchases` (dynamically required)
- Product IDs: `portiontrack.monthly`, `portiontrack.annual`
- Fallback prices hardcoded: `$3.99/mo`, `$29.99/yr`
- Flow: `initializeStoreKit()` → `connectAsync()` + `setPurchaseListener()` → `queryProducts()` → `purchaseItemAsync()`
- On successful purchase: `saveSubscriptionStatus(true)` to AsyncStorage + `emitSubscriptionUpdate(true)` to context
- `restorePurchases()` checks `getPurchaseHistoryAsync()` for either product ID
- `checkAppStoreSubscription()` also uses purchase history (not a live receipt check)
- **No server-side receipt validation** (noted as TODO)

---

## Summary of the full onboarding/paywall flow

```
App launch
  ├── hasProfile = false  →  welcome.tsx
  │     └── "Start Free Trial" → PaywallScreen modal
  │           └── purchase success → emitSubscriptionUpdate(true)
  │                 → SubscriptionContext.isSubscribed = true
  │                       → useEffect → router.replace('/setup-profile') or '/(tabs)/(home)'
  │
  └── hasProfile = true   →  (tabs) directly  ← NO subscription check (production gap)

DEV mode: isSubscribed is always true → welcome.tsx immediately redirects to (tabs)/(home) or setup-profile
```

